# Enums (wire shorts)

Put all shared enums in `lib/core/enums/`.

Use field-based enhanced Dart enums: `@JsonValue` + a `const` constructor
with an explicit `wireValue` (and any per-value data as `final` fields),
plus a `fromWire` lookup over `values`:

```dart
enum SubscriptionPlan {
  @JsonValue(0)
  standard(wireValue: 0, label: 'STANDARD'),
  @JsonValue(1)
  premium(wireValue: 1, label: 'PREMIUM');

  const SubscriptionPlan({required this.wireValue, required this.label});

  final int wireValue;
  final String label;

  static SubscriptionPlan? fromWire(int? value) {
    for (final plan in values) {
      if (plan.wireValue == value) return plan;
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

- Never derive `wireValue` from `index`; reordering values would change the wire.
- Prefer `final` fields over `switch (this)` getters for per-value data.
- Plain enums with only `@JsonValue` (no members) don't need fields.

## Known ordinals

| Enum | Wire |
|------|------|
| `SubscriptionPlan` | 0 STANDARD, 1 PREMIUM |
| `SubscriptionStatus` | 0 ACTIVE … 3 REVOKED |
| `SubscriptionSource` | 0 REVENUECAT, 1 MANUAL |
| `Entitlement` | 0 VIDEO, 1 LIVE |
| `ActivityType` | 0 VIDEO, 1 LIVE |
| `LiveProvider` | 0 ZOOM |
| `QuizStatus` | 0–2 |

JSON models keep `int` / `List<int>` and map with `fromWire` in `toEntity()`.
Do not treat plan/status/source/entitlements as wire strings.
